  "notes": [
    "An unrelated EOA redeemed other holders' rfETH and rfDAI shares about nine hours before the main attacker; the owners were EOAs that never approved anyone. Sibling ReaperVaultV2 deployments (rfUSDC, rfWFTM, rfBTC, rfDAI, rfUSDT) were drained in the same campaign and are described here, not as targets.",
    "Campaign: every unauthorised redeem by unaffiliated parties until the vaults were empty, found from Withdraw logs with caller != owner; no vault ever emitted an Approval. Redeems by vault strategist 0x1e71aee6 and co-signer 0x60bc5e04 into their Safe 0x539ef36c are an affiliated rescue and excluded.",
    "Loss is the underlying paid out by those redeems. DefiLlama was unavailable, so ETH, BTC and FTM use CoinGecko hourly prices at each block and the bridged stablecoins are at par."
  ]
